<!-- ABSTRACT -->
<h1>ABSTRACT</h1>

<p>
  Image and document intelligence combined with generative large language models (LLMs) provide unprecedented capabilities to revolutionize personalized education, active recall, and diagnostic self-assessment. Traditional study approaches often suffer from passive rereading, lack of immediate feedback, and disconnected assessment tools.
</p>
<p>
  This project presents <strong>CogniLearn</strong>, an autonomous, end-to-end generative AI educational platform capable of transforming raw academic text and multi-page PDF documents into comprehensive pedagogical study materials and rigorous diagnostic evaluations. Powered by Google's state-of-the-art <strong>Gemini Flash</strong> multimodal model via the <code>@google/genai</code> TypeScript SDK and Python SDK, the platform implements strict JSON schema enforcement to produce structured curriculum outputs, including:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>Executive summaries with foundational mental models and learning objectives;</li>
  <li>Modular curriculum breakdowns with Feynman-style analogies, real-world case studies, and common pitfall warnings;</li>
  <li>High-yield cheat sheets featuring crucial definitions, formulas, and mnemonics;</li>
  <li>3D interactive flashcards optimized for active recall;</li>
  <li>Multi-format diagnostic question suites comprising multiple-choice questions (MCQs), clinical/applied scenario cases, true/false conceptual checks, and open-ended short answers with real-time automated rubric scoring.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  To support longitudinal retention, CogniLearn incorporates a <strong>Smart Study Scheduler</strong> based on Ebbinghaus' forgetting curve, actively tracking study intervals and issuing automated alerts when a deck exceeds 24 hours without review. The system is engineered as a dual-architecture deployment: a high-performance full-stack TypeScript/React SPA running on Express and Vite, alongside a native Python Streamlit application designed for rapid cloud deployment. Latency optimization techniques—such as parallelized asynchronous generation, prompt minimization, and transient error backoff mechanisms—reduce generation latency to under 5 seconds for focused question suites.
</p>

<p><strong>Keywords:</strong> Generative AI, Large Language Models, Gemini Flash, Automated Question Generation, Active Recall, Spaced Repetition, Streamlit, React, TypeScript, IFHE.</p>

<p><strong>PROJECT AIM:</strong> The objective of this project is to architect, develop, and benchmark an automated generative AI platform that converts arbitrary academic documents into structured pedagogical learning materials, interactive flashcards, and diagnostic question banks with real-time AI-guided scoring and spaced review scheduling.</p>

